  ],
  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "ACCRINT uses plain binary64 day-count steps with canonical period normalization and an x87 PC64 final coupon multiply",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20131, 20228, and 20527, ACCRINT(issue, first_interest, settlement, rate, [par], frequency, [basis], [calc_method]) evaluates day-count fractions in plain binary64 arithmetic normalized by the canonical last coupon period CoupDays(first - 1 period, first) rather than the settlement period's actual length, sums calc_method=TRUE (default) walks backward from settlement to issue, skips whole interior coupon periods when calc_method=FALSE and issue precedes that canonical period, and applies an x87 PC64 multiply followed by binary64 rounding only at the final coupon * accrual product. Matches 146,688/146,688 full-bank and 120/120 pinned ACCRINT rows.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across 146,688 full-bank and 120 pinned ACCRINT rows in Excel 16.0 builds 20131 and 20228 (witnesses/ACCRINT.json) and Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (row 344) and f3_financial (row 16).",
